<html><head><title>Quillmoor ledger</title></head><body><article><h1>Quillmoor ledger</h1><p>The harbour ledger of Quillmoor records that the night ferry left at a quarter past nine on every weekday of the winter season.</p><p>Its keeper, Odalys Brenn, wrote each departure in green ink and each delay in red, so that a reader could count the late crossings at a glance.</p><p>In the third winter the ferry ran late on forty-one nights, most of them in the weeks when fog lay over the eastern breakwater.</p><p>The town council answered by moving the departure to half past eight, which cut the late crossings to nine in the winter that followed.</p><p>日本語の段落もある。港の帳簿は町の図書館に今も保管されている。</p><p>Filler paragraph number 0 keeps the extractor sure that this page is an article with running text enough to be worth reading, sentence after sentence.</p><p>Filler paragraph number 1 keeps the extractor sure that this page is an article with running text enough to be worth reading, sentence after sentence.</p><p>Filler paragraph number 2 keeps the extractor sure that this page is an article with running text enough to be worth reading, sentence after sentence.</p><p>Filler paragraph number 3 keeps the extractor sure that this page is an article with running text enough to be worth reading, sentence after sentence.</p><p>Filler paragraph number 4 keeps the extractor sure that this page is an article with running text enough to be worth reading, sentence after sentence.</p><p>Filler paragraph number 5 keeps the extractor sure that this page is an article with running text enough to be worth reading, sentence after sentence.</p><p>Filler paragraph number 6 keeps the extractor sure that this page is an article with running text enough to be worth reading, sentence after sentence.</p><p>Filler paragraph number 7 keeps the extractor sure that this page is an article with running text enough to be worth reading, sentence after sentence.</p></article></body></html>